FILED s536f (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08), the residue of #4581 (scratch/s536f/p/m2.pl row 4, p/m2b.pl rows 4-5 in the s536f worktree).  PRE-EXISTING: main c8886b61 answers the same.

REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3):

    my $x = "x"; my $v = "vw"; my @b = (1, 2);
    for ($x, substr($v,1), @b) { $_ .= "+" } print "1 $x $v @b\n";
    my $w = "ww"; my $y = "yy";
    for (substr($w, 0, 1), substr $y, 1) { $_ = "M" } print "2 $w $y\n";
    my $p = "pp"; my $q = "qq"; $p =~ /p/g; $q =~ /q/g;
    for (pos $p, pos $q) { $_ = 0 } print "3 ", pos($p), pos($q), "\n";

perl: `1 x+ vw+ 1+ 2+` / `2 Mw yM` / `3 00`.   PCL: `1 x+ vw 1+ 2+` / `2 ww yy` / `3 11`.

WHY (read): s536f's #4581 lets a magic-lvalue call be one element of the `(vector ...)` foreach shape -- the shape for lists whose every element is ONE value (Pl::Parser::_foreach_scalar_elements).  Row 1 holds an array, so the list goes through the run-time flattener (`p-flatten-args`), where the substr is lowered as a value; the per-element alias rewrite would have to reach the element inside the flattened list (a magic CELL is a box the flattener keeps as one element, so swapping the head there is enough -- the mapping from elements to the lowered list's arguments is the work).  Rows 2-3: the shared #138 comma splitter (`lowprec_split_safe`) declines a run that starts with a Word before a comma (the paren-less list operator may swallow it), so the whole list declines; a paren-less `substr` / `vec` would have to take the REST of the list as its one element.


=== DONE (s536i) ===
a magic-lvalue call in a flattened foreach list (an array among the elements, a paren-less `substr $y, 1` / `pos $q` among several) and in a map / grep list is its write-through cell: %p-aliasing-slice-form gains `p-substr` (<= 3 args) / `p-pos` / `p-vec` -> `-lvalue-cell` over the target's place (%p-magic-lvalue-alias-form, %p-alias-place-form; the element `-box` head map %p-elem-box-head shared with the element arm).  VarAnnotator: _ev_foreach_magic_args DELETED, folded into the ONE foreach slot walk (_ev_foreach_magic_slot) -- both spellings, the modifier form too; map / grep list operands get _tw_alias_list_operands, which also fixed a pre-existing unfiled `map { $_ .= "X" } $x` with a raw-slot $x (without it the new cell DIED read-only there).  Guard Pl/t/lvalue-ref-01.t row 23 (fails on 3139fcb0).  Commit: subject `s536i WIP #4684`.
